+# Handoff Summary — Floating-Apps
+
+Paste the sections below into a new coding session (or apply manually). Everything
+below was implemented and verified by static analysis, but could NOT be pushed to
+GitHub because the previous session was closed and remote access was blocked.
+
+## Repository / branch context
+
+- Repo: `JohnOlowe/Floating-Apps`
+- Base: `main` @ `15ab1ec` ("Merge pull request #4 from JohnOlowe/arena/01a0337d-floating-apps")
+- Work branch: `arena/01a057a3-floating-apps`
+- Language/build: Android app, Java 11, Kotlin DSL Gradle, AGP 8.0.0, Gradle 8.5,
+  compileSdk 33, targetSdk 33, minSdk 19 (Android 4.4).
+- App uses AndroidX (appcompat 1.6.1, material 1.9.0, constraintlayout 2.1.4).
+
+## Goal
+
+Two things were requested:
+1. Home-screen tiles should be the teal/"greenish-purple" (`#00aaaa`) shade in BOTH
+   light and dark themes (they were grey `#aaa` in light mode).
+2. Fix "Open in another app" in the floating PDF reader, which always showed an
+   error.
+3. (Later) Make the app fully usable on Android 4.4 (API 19) — this is the bigger
+   goal and is partially done (see "Android 4.4 status" below).
+
+---
+
+## Change 1 — Home-screen tile color (DONE)
+
+`app/src/main/res/values/colors.xml`:
+```
+<color name="buttonColor">#00aaaa</color>   <!-- was #aaa -->
+```
+
+`app/src/main/res/layout/activity_main.xml` (calculator tile):
+```
+android:background="@color/buttonColor"     <!-- was "#00aaaa" hardcoded -->
+```
+
+Note: `buttonColor` is also used by the other floating screens (bible, calculator,
+PDF, notes, player, timer, captions), so those all become teal in light mode too.
+If you only want the HOME SCREEN changed, use a dedicated color instead of
+reusing `buttonColor`.
+
+---
+
+## Change 2 — PDF "Open in another app" fix (DONE)
+
+File: `app/src/main/java/damjay/floating/projects/PDFReaderService.java`
+
+Root cause: the app-chooser was built and shown directly from a `Service`:
+`new AlertDialog.Builder(service).show()`. A `Service` has no window token, so
+`show()` throws `BadTokenException`, which was swallowed by a `catch (Exception)`
+and surfaced as "An error occurred". Also, `startActivity()` from a Service needs
+`FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK`.
+
+Fix applied:
+1. Add `FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK` to the open intent:
+```java
+openIntent.addFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK);
+```
+2. Build the dialog with `.create()`, set its window type to an overlay type, then
+   `.show()`:
+```java
+android.app.AlertDialog chooserDialog =
+        new android.app.AlertDialog.Builder(PDFReaderService.this)
+                .setTitle(R.string.choose_app_to_open)
+                .setItems(labels.toArray(new String[0]), (dialog, which) -> { ... })
+                .setNegativeButton(android.R.string.cancel, null)
+                .create();
+
+if (chooserDialog.getWindow() != null) {
+    if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.O) {
+        chooserDialog.getWindow().setType(
+                WindowManager.LayoutParams.TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY);
+    } else {
+        chooserDialog.getWindow().setType(
+                WindowManager.LayoutParams.TYPE_SYSTEM_ALERT);
+    }
+}
+chooserDialog.show();
+```
+
+---
+
+## Change 3 — Android 4.4 (API 19) compatibility (PARTIALLY DONE)
+
+Static analysis (equivalent to lint `NewApi`) found these blockers. Status:
+
+### 3a. Vector drawables rasterization (DONE — was a guaranteed crash on 4.4)
+
+`app/build.gradle.kts`: REMOVE the `vectorDrawables { useSupportLibrary = true }`
+block inside `defaultConfig`. With it removed, AGP rasterizes the vector icons
+(`play`, `pause`, `plus`, `minus`, `cancel`, `fast_forward`, `fast_backward`,
+`copy_logo`) to PNG for pre-21 devices. Without this, the floating service layouts
+(calculator, music, PDF, notes) crash on API 19 because `VectorDrawable` is API 21+.
+
+Delete file: `app/src/main/res/drawable-anydpi/copy_logo.xml` (a stray non-v21
+vector; `copy_logo` already has PNGs in every density bucket plus a v21 vector in
+`drawable-anydpi-v21/`).
+
+### 3b. Clicker "clicked device" mode guard (DONE)
+
+`app/src/main/java/damjay/floating/projects/autoclicker/activity/ActionSelectorActivity.java`
+
+`GestureDescription` / `dispatchGesture()` are API 24 (Android 7.0)+. Guard
+`startAccessibilityService()` so the class is never loaded on older devices:
+```java
+if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT < Build.VERSION_CODES.N) {
+    Toast.makeText(this, R.string.clicker_service_not_supported, Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show();
+    return;
+}
+```
+Add imports `android.os.Build` and `android.widget.Toast`.
+
+Added string (values/strings.xml):
+```xml
+<string name="clicker_service_not_supported">The &#8220;clicked device&#8221; mode requires Android 7.0 (Nougat) or higher. You can still use this device as the controller.</string>
+```
+
+### 3c. PDF entry-point guards (DONE)
+
+`PdfRenderer` is API 21 (Android 5.0)+. Two entry points were unguarded:
+
+1. `app/src/main/java/damjay/floating/projects/QuickLaunchControl.java` — the
+   calculator's quick-launch PDF button. Guard:
+```java
+if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT < Build.VERSION_CODES.LOLLIPOP) {
+    Toast.makeText(appContext, R.string.pdf_not_supported, Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show();
+    return;
+}
+```
+Add imports `android.os.Build`, `android.widget.Toast`.
+
+2. `app/src/main/java/damjay/floating/projects/FloatingPDFActivity.java` — a
+   `VIEW` intent from another app. Guard at the top of `onCreate()`:
+```java
+if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT < Build.VERSION_CODES.LOLLIPOP) {
+    Toast.makeText(this, R.string.pdf_not_supported, Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show();
+    finish();
+    return;
+}
+```
+(The home-screen PDF tile in `MainActivity` was ALREADY guarded with the same
+message.)
+
+The existing string `pdf_not_supported` reads: "Sorry, PDF Reader is only
+available on phones running Android 5 and higher."
+
+### 3d. NOT DONE — in-app PDF rendering on Android 4.4 (OPEN DECISION)
+
+The native `PdfRenderer` is API 21+. On Android 4.4 there is currently no in-app
+PDF rendering (it falls back to the "not supported" message). A library fallback
+was requested but hit a hard constraint:
+
+- Native `android.graphics.pdf.PdfRenderer` = API 21+.
+- `io.legere:pdfiumandroid` (PdfiumAndroidKt) — the engine behind the maintained
+  `dev.zwander:pdfviewer` AndroidX fork — is documented as ">= API 21".
+- `com.github.barteksc:android-pdf-viewer:3.2.0-beta.1` was "updated to support
+  library 28" — it is a SUPPORT-LIBRARY artifact that conflicts with this
+  project's AndroidX + AGP 8 (jetifier was removed in AGP 8).
+- The only AndroidX fork with an API 11+ engine is
+  `com.github.TalbotGooday:AndroidPdfViewer` via **JitPack**, last updated ~4 years
+  ago, bundling old pdfium native libs with a 16 KB page-size issue Google flags.
+
+Recommended: keep native `PdfRenderer` on Android 5+, and either (a) accept the
+"not supported" fallback on 4.4, or (b) deliberately add the JitPack fork knowing
+it is unmaintained. Do NOT add the barteksc Maven Central artifact (support-lib
+conflict).
+
